# Signing material / release config — never commit (a leaked keystore password
# can't be un-leaked by a later commit; a lost release keystore permanently
# orphans the Play Store listing). Keep backups outside this repo.
*.jks
*.keystore
key.properties
*.p12
node_modules/
firestore-debug.log
firebase-debug.log
ui-debug.log

# Claude dev-team — local-only state (see planning/claude-dev-team.md).
# The merge-gate markers are ephemeral. The subagent journal is excluded too: it
# holds raw subagent output, which shouldn't land permanently in the history of a
# repo that touches real health data. /standup still reads it from the working copy.
.claude/team/review-verdict.md
.claude/team/last-green
.claude/team/log/*
!.claude/team/log/.gitkeep

# Live identifiers (project id, household/pet doc ids, Auth uids) — local only. Anything in a
# public repo's history is permanent; see planning/claude-dev-team.md "Nothing live goes in git".
.claude/local/
# Git worktrees the team creates per issue — each is its own checkout, never part of this one.
.claude/worktrees/

# Migration tooling (tools/migrate/ — read its README). Neither of these may ever be committed.
# A dump is a complete, unencrypted copy of two people's health record; the service-account key is
# unrestricted read/write on the live project. security-privacy.md §2.1/§2.3 treats both as assets
# equivalent to the database itself, and a leak cannot be undone by a later commit.
tools/migrate/dumps/
dump-*.json
*service-account*.json
*serviceAccount*.json
